WEBVTT

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:04.410
With money, you could make life 
easier for all those close to you.

00:00:04.410 --> 00:00:06.790
Don't you want to take good 
care of your parents?

00:00:06.790 --> 00:00:09.730
Of course I do, but...

00:00:09.730 --> 00:00:12.100
Then do it. Get into show business.

00:00:12.310 --> 00:00:13.380
Hey—

00:00:12.620 --> 00:00:15.160
As I've told you several times now,

00:00:15.160 --> 00:00:17.080
I came here today to decline—

00:00:17.080 --> 00:00:20.320
Shida-chan, you're no fun at all.

00:00:20.320 --> 00:00:22.420
Maybe your parents didn't raise you right?

00:00:35.780 --> 00:00:38.400
Don't you dare make fun 
of my childhood friend.

00:00:45.270 --> 00:00:48.760
Tch! I had a bad feeling when you 
showed up with all this trash.

00:00:48.760 --> 00:00:49.950
Guess I was right!

00:00:50.580 --> 00:00:51.890
Are you trash, too?!

00:00:54.630 --> 00:00:57.310
Yo, what the hell did you just say?!

00:00:57.310 --> 00:00:59.830
Wait... Tetsuhiko-kun! If you do that—

00:00:59.830 --> 00:01:01.360
Tetsuhiko, stop!

00:01:01.360 --> 00:01:03.090
Let go of me, Dumbharu!

00:01:03.090 --> 00:01:06.400
I'm not gonna let this asshole 
make fun of my friend!

00:01:06.400 --> 00:01:07.590
Tetsuhiko...

00:01:07.800 --> 00:01:09.280
Bunch of trash.

00:01:08.350 --> 00:01:09.580
Let go!

00:01:10.230 --> 00:01:11.190
Damn it!

00:01:11.190 --> 00:01:11.960
You can't!

00:01:12.410 --> 00:01:14.700
Hey, call the police.

00:01:14.700 --> 00:01:16.700
A little hoodlum's attacking me.

00:01:18.740 --> 00:01:21.160
What did you say? I'll be right there!

00:01:22.590 --> 00:01:25.150
All of you, stay right here!

00:01:26.400 --> 00:01:27.840
What do we do now?!

00:01:27.840 --> 00:01:29.670
I didn't hurt him.

00:01:29.670 --> 00:01:31.720
We're the only ones in here.

00:01:31.720 --> 00:01:33.980
We all just need to testify 
that nothing happened.

00:01:33.980 --> 00:01:35.470
And what about the wine?

00:01:35.470 --> 00:01:36.980
There's no missing that.

00:01:37.230 --> 00:01:41.330
Just say that moron tripped and 
dumped it all over his own head.

00:01:41.330 --> 00:01:42.550
Of course!

00:01:42.550 --> 00:01:45.370
This is the first time you've 
seemed so reliable to me!

00:01:45.640 --> 00:01:47.810
I'll testify that way, too.

00:01:47.810 --> 00:01:49.940
I mean, he's just too much.

00:01:49.940 --> 00:01:51.720
And if necessary, I'll—

00:01:51.720 --> 00:01:52.500
Hold it.

00:01:53.240 --> 00:01:55.480
Haru, as your big sister,

00:01:55.480 --> 00:01:59.450
I think making everyone lie about the 
wine I threw at him is going too far.

00:01:59.450 --> 00:02:00.550
Well, I guess...

00:02:00.550 --> 00:02:03.710
And the idea of going back 
into show business...

00:02:03.710 --> 00:02:05.870
It's gonna be tough now, huh?

00:02:05.870 --> 00:02:09.420
He'll probably go around spreading 
a lot of half-truths,

00:02:09.420 --> 00:02:12.030
which will make other agencies wary, too.

00:02:12.340 --> 00:02:14.130
Haru, you're such an idiot.

00:02:12.670 --> 00:02:14.130
What happened?

00:02:14.130 --> 00:02:17.530
Allow me to explain that.

00:02:20.360 --> 00:02:22.660
Well, you sure have grown up, Maru-chan.

00:02:22.660 --> 00:02:26.740
Remember me? I'm Kachi Souichirou 
of Kozuka Pharmaceuticals.

00:02:26.740 --> 00:02:29.570
Or maybe you'd remember 
me better as Shiro's dad?

00:02:30.580 --> 00:02:32.340
I-It's good to see you again!

00:02:32.340 --> 00:02:34.820
You're the one making the commercial?

00:02:34.820 --> 00:02:36.560
You're here, too, Shiro?

00:02:36.560 --> 00:02:38.040
And all of you?

00:02:38.700 --> 00:02:43.080
Could you explain what happened 
in a way that I can understand?

00:02:44.050 --> 00:02:49.020
Osamake: Romcom Where
The Childhood Friend Won't Lose

00:02:50.370 --> 00:02:52.970
I see. So that's what happened.

00:02:53.460 --> 00:02:56.090
Haru said what he said for my sake.

00:02:56.090 --> 00:02:58.660
So just call it my fault.

00:02:58.660 --> 00:02:59.630
Kuro...

00:03:00.460 --> 00:03:03.480
I know how you feel, 
but that's not the issue.

00:03:03.480 --> 00:03:05.170
You understand, don't you?

00:03:07.100 --> 00:03:11.570
I'm also convinced that Su-chan did 
the right thing as human being.

00:03:11.570 --> 00:03:15.630
So no matter what the law says,
 I'll back Su-chan.

00:03:15.630 --> 00:03:17.920
I know how you feel, too, but...

00:03:18.200 --> 00:03:22.280
Who decided that the only way 
to hurt someone is physically?

00:03:22.720 --> 00:03:24.800
Words are sharp blades, too.

00:03:25.160 --> 00:03:28.620
And he hurt all of us with his verbal blades.

00:03:28.620 --> 00:03:30.670
Su-chan was only protecting us.

00:03:32.320 --> 00:03:34.900
Considering all of your opinions together,

00:03:34.900 --> 00:03:38.070
my conviction compels me to 
support Sueharu-oniichan,

00:03:38.070 --> 00:03:40.460
so I would like this to 
be resolved peacefully.

00:03:40.460 --> 00:03:42.150
Would that be all right?

00:03:42.410 --> 00:03:45.470
But of course, Shun-san, 
you won't agree with that.

00:03:45.470 --> 00:03:46.590
Damn right I won't!

00:03:46.590 --> 00:03:48.500
I'm the victim here! Me!

00:03:49.250 --> 00:03:50.270
You're—

00:03:50.270 --> 00:03:51.450
Don't, Tetsuhiko.

00:03:51.820 --> 00:03:53.200
Well, then...

00:03:53.640 --> 00:03:56.180
Why don't we have a commercial contest?

00:03:57.420 --> 00:03:58.630
Uh... Momo?

00:03:58.900 --> 00:04:03.990
Shun-san, if you involve the police, 
Sueharu-oniichan won't join your agency, right?

00:04:03.990 --> 00:04:06.580
Which means, naturally, 
there'll be no profit for you.

00:04:06.580 --> 00:04:09.670
That isn't really what you want, is it?

00:04:10.090 --> 00:04:11.150
That's true.

00:04:11.560 --> 00:04:13.470
So here's my suggestion.

00:04:13.470 --> 00:04:14.960
We'll have a commercial contest.

00:04:14.960 --> 00:04:18.160
If you win, Sueharu-oniichan 
will join your agency

00:04:18.160 --> 00:04:20.890
and do whatever work you want him to.

00:04:20.890 --> 00:04:23.310
But if Sueharu-oniichan wins,

00:04:23.310 --> 00:04:25.610
you won't file a police report,

00:04:25.610 --> 00:04:27.680
and even if he tries to join another agency,

00:04:27.680 --> 00:04:30.080
you won't do anything to 
interfere with his decision.

00:04:30.080 --> 00:04:31.530
That works for you, right?

00:04:35.320 --> 00:04:37.300
Okay. That's fine.

00:04:37.490 --> 00:04:40.580
Sir, would you mind if we 
made two proposals for the commercial

00:04:40.580 --> 00:04:42.520
you wanted Sueharu-oniichan 
to do if he came back,

00:04:42.520 --> 00:04:46.610
one produced by the agency's side and 
one produced by Onii-chan's side?

00:04:46.610 --> 00:04:49.730
Sure. That itself should 
draw a lot of attention.

00:04:49.730 --> 00:04:53.210
What do you say, Sueharu-oniichan? 
Will you compete?

00:04:53.210 --> 00:04:54.020
Yeah, I'll do it.

00:04:54.460 --> 00:04:57.720
Then we'll set up a special site 
to post the two commercials on.

00:04:57.720 --> 00:04:59.620
The viewers will vote on them,

00:04:59.620 --> 00:05:02.770
and the one that gets the most 
votes wins. How does that sound?

00:05:02.960 --> 00:05:05.240
Haru won't stand a chance!

00:05:05.240 --> 00:05:07.030
Even he can't do all that by himself!

00:05:07.230 --> 00:05:10.900
Onii-chan told me earlier about 
the Ultramarine Channel.

00:05:10.900 --> 00:05:13.460
He said it was Tetsuhiko-san's idea.

00:05:13.460 --> 00:05:17.030
I think it sounds wonderful. 
Such a perfect teenage activity.

00:05:17.030 --> 00:05:18.790
I kind of admire that.

00:05:19.240 --> 00:05:24.900
Perhaps you could call the members of the 
Ultramarine Channel the "Ultramarine Alliance"?

00:05:24.900 --> 00:05:27.800
With these members, I think 
you'd stand a very good chance.

00:05:27.800 --> 00:05:38.400
<b>Commercial Contest Rules</b>

00:05:27.800 --> 00:05:38.400
<b>The original budget allotted for the</b>

00:05:27.800 --> 00:05:38.400
<b>commercial will be divided evenly between</b>

00:05:27.800 --> 00:05:38.400
<b>both production teams, and Kozuka Pharmaceuticals</b>

00:05:27.800 --> 00:05:38.400
<b>will create the site both commercials</b>

00:05:27.800 --> 00:05:38.400
<b>will be published on.</b>

00:05:28.890 --> 00:05:31.310
The contest will begin in one 
week and last three days.

00:05:31.310 --> 00:05:36.130
A shorter work period will prevent the 
agency from hiring a production team,

00:05:36.130 --> 00:05:38.410
putting both sides on more even footing.

00:05:38.700 --> 00:05:41.620
I'm willing to give them 
that much of a handicap.

00:05:41.620 --> 00:05:47.760
Sir, can we ask you to help Sueharu-oniichan's
 team get the staff they need?

00:05:47.760 --> 00:05:48.700
I'll arrange it.

00:05:48.960 --> 00:05:52.260
Now the conditions for both 
teams are basically equal.

00:05:52.260 --> 00:05:54.430
I just want to make sure of one thing.

00:05:54.430 --> 00:05:56.380
Will you be in our commercial, Momo?

00:05:56.380 --> 00:05:59.450
I want to show you how much 
I've grown in six years,

00:05:59.450 --> 00:06:02.090
so I'm planning to appear 
in Shun-san's commercial.

00:06:02.090 --> 00:06:05.380
Bu—I was really counting on your 
fame to give us a boost, though!

00:06:05.680 --> 00:06:08.400
My life depends on this! Please don't!

00:06:08.400 --> 00:06:09.380
Haru...

00:06:09.380 --> 00:06:10.430
Su-chan...

00:06:10.430 --> 00:06:13.260
Groveling is not what you should 
be doing after all this.

00:06:13.490 --> 00:06:15.230
I'll do my very best!

00:06:16.450 --> 00:06:18.400
How does that sound?

00:06:18.400 --> 00:06:19.230
Wait.

00:06:19.910 --> 00:06:22.390
There's one more condition I'd like to add.

00:06:24.970 --> 00:06:30.630
Momo, are you sure you didn't want to add the 
condition that you'd quit the agency if I won?

00:06:30.630 --> 00:06:31.280
Huh?

00:06:31.660 --> 00:06:34.030
You asked me to save you before.

00:06:34.280 --> 00:06:36.610
You meant from that president, didn't you?

00:06:36.920 --> 00:06:38.540
Thank you for mentioning that.

00:06:38.740 --> 00:06:41.100
I'll add that condition in secret later.

00:06:45.260 --> 00:06:48.150
The first round table meeting 
of the entertainment club,

00:06:45.590 --> 00:06:50.430
Sports Drink 
<b>AquaMine</b>

00:06:48.150 --> 00:06:50.430
A.K.A. Ultramarine Alliance, will now begin.

00:06:50.430 --> 00:07:01.940
<b>First Round-Table Meeting
 of the Ultramarine Alliance</b>

00:06:50.750 --> 00:06:52.970
Our topic is the commercial contest.

00:06:52.970 --> 00:06:57.030
The product being promoted is a sports 
drink to be released in the future.

00:06:57.030 --> 00:07:00.060
Kachi's dad has said he wants 
to sell it to young people,

00:07:00.060 --> 00:07:01.930
so we should keep it youthful.

00:07:02.310 --> 00:07:05.560
Kachi, can you let us in on 
your vision for this contest?

00:07:05.560 --> 00:07:08.430
You're psyched for the chance 
to realize your dream, right?

00:07:08.600 --> 00:07:12.600
If we can execute the plan,
 I was up all night thinking about,

00:07:13.210 --> 00:07:14.300
we can win.

00:07:14.950 --> 00:07:19.960
<b>Osamake: Romcom Where
The Childhood Friend Won't Lose</b>

00:07:14.950 --> 00:07:19.960
<b>Episode 6
The One Who Laughs Last</b>

00:07:14.950 --> 00:07:19.960
Oh, really?
We've won, then.

00:07:14.950 --> 00:07:19.960
<b>Glint</b>

00:07:14.950 --> 00:07:19.960
<b>Click</b>

00:07:14.950 --> 00:07:19.960
He's trying
so hard to
look cool.

00:07:22.270 --> 00:07:24.850
<i>I hated everything.</i>

00:07:24.850 --> 00:07:26.730
<i>Everything but my older sister.</i>

00:07:27.590 --> 00:07:30.170
I promise I'll protect you, Maria.

00:07:30.170 --> 00:07:31.600
Onee-chan...

00:07:32.200 --> 00:07:34.560
<i>When she graduated from middle school,</i>

00:07:34.560 --> 00:07:36.710
<i>the two of us ran away from home.</i>

00:07:37.570 --> 00:07:40.630
<i>Despite her excellent grades, 
my sister didn't go on to college.</i>

00:07:40.630 --> 00:07:43.560
<i>She put all her effort 
into working to raise me.</i>

00:07:44.390 --> 00:07:46.470
<i>I hated it.</i>

00:07:46.470 --> 00:07:49.020
<i>I hated everything in the 
world that made her suffer,</i>

00:07:49.440 --> 00:07:52.800
<i>and I hated my powerless 
self for holding her back.</i>

00:07:54.630 --> 00:07:59.000
<i>One day, I was scouted by the agency's
president at that time, Nina Hardy.</i>

00:07:59.270 --> 00:08:01.560
<i>I joined the agency, 
hoping it would make things</i>

00:08:01.560 --> 00:08:03.730
<i>at least a little bit easier for my sister.</i>

00:08:04.170 --> 00:08:06.820
<i>It was there that I met Sueharu-oniichan,</i>

00:08:06.820 --> 00:08:08.620
<i>my destined one.</i>

00:08:10.710 --> 00:08:13.420
You always look so timid.

00:08:13.420 --> 00:08:15.210
Is it fun to live like that?

00:08:15.670 --> 00:08:17.910
I'm not like you.

00:08:17.910 --> 00:08:20.990
I wasn't blessed with good 
fortune like you are!

00:08:20.990 --> 00:08:22.550
No matter what I do, it's...

00:08:22.880 --> 00:08:25.810
Is it really useless? Are you sure?

00:08:25.810 --> 00:08:27.980
When you haven't even put your 
full strength into it yet?

00:08:27.980 --> 00:08:30.030
You don't think you'll regret that?

00:08:30.510 --> 00:08:33.000
You don't have to tell me that!

00:08:33.000 --> 00:08:34.380
But... But...

00:08:34.380 --> 00:08:35.990
No buts!

00:08:36.230 --> 00:08:38.350
Ow!

00:08:40.020 --> 00:08:41.700
Give it all of your strength!

00:08:41.700 --> 00:08:43.490
You have talent!

00:08:43.760 --> 00:08:47.290
Plus, you're smarter than me, 
and you have better intuition.

00:08:47.290 --> 00:08:49.780
Of course, you can't top 
me in acting, though!

00:08:50.040 --> 00:08:51.800
R-Really?

00:08:52.300 --> 00:08:53.990
I guarantee it.

00:08:54.270 --> 00:08:55.770
So grow up.

00:08:59.240 --> 00:09:02.090
Okay. I'll try my best.

00:09:02.090 --> 00:09:04.520
I'll try hard enough to catch up to you.

00:09:04.520 --> 00:09:06.350
Will you wait for me until then?

00:09:06.760 --> 00:09:07.940
Of course I will.

00:09:08.930 --> 00:09:13.570
<i>Onii-chan's shining light 
saved me from the darkness.</i>

00:09:13.830 --> 00:09:16.200
<i>But one day, out of the blue...</i>

00:09:16.770 --> 00:09:20.640
You're amazing, Onii-chan! You're a hero!

00:09:20.640 --> 00:09:23.290
There's no way you can give up acting!

00:09:23.490 --> 00:09:25.160
Onii-chan!

00:09:25.160 --> 00:09:27.800
Sueharu-oniichan!

00:09:28.750 --> 00:09:31.040
<i>Even when you're standing 
on a dazzling stage,</i>

00:09:31.040 --> 00:09:32.650
<i>it's lonely by yourself.</i>

00:09:33.020 --> 00:09:36.020
<i>I'm still within the darkness.</i>

00:09:39.220 --> 00:09:40.650
I'm home.

00:09:40.650 --> 00:09:42.190
Welcome back, Onee-chan.

00:09:42.190 --> 00:09:44.880
I brought home a meal from work.
 Let's eat it together.

00:09:44.880 --> 00:09:47.270
You don't need to work part-time, you know.

00:09:47.270 --> 00:09:49.830
You should enjoy your college life more.

00:09:49.830 --> 00:09:52.850
It's more than enough that you're 
helping me pay my tuition.

00:09:53.120 --> 00:09:55.270
The commercial contest is today, right?

00:09:55.270 --> 00:09:58.240
You told me not to watch your commercial,

00:09:58.240 --> 00:09:59.810
but I did anyway. Sorry.

00:09:59.810 --> 00:10:03.290
You shouldn't have watched it!
 It's too embarrassing!

00:10:05.820 --> 00:10:08.120
I liked it. It had a classic feel to it.

00:10:08.120 --> 00:10:09.840
Our side is more capable,

00:10:09.840 --> 00:10:14.860
so the idea was that a popular actress 
and high video quality should be enough.

00:10:14.860 --> 00:10:16.750
It's how the ruling class fights.

00:10:16.750 --> 00:10:21.100
Well, let's check out your beloved 
Sueharu-oniichan's video now.

00:10:21.100 --> 00:10:21.970
Wait!

00:10:22.210 --> 00:10:23.490
What is it?

00:10:26.800 --> 00:10:29.830
I'm okay. Go ahead, Onee-chan.

00:10:29.830 --> 00:10:30.860
All right.

00:10:31.110 --> 00:10:33.070
<b>Enjoy Your Youth!!</b>

00:10:31.110 --> 00:10:33.070
<b>AquaMine</b>

00:10:33.460 --> 00:10:35.500
<i>Ugh, I'm so bored.</i>

00:10:35.500 --> 00:10:38.150
<i>C'mon, Sueharu, how dumb can you be?</i>

00:10:38.150 --> 00:10:42.070
<i>You only get one life, and one 
shot at being a high schooler.</i>

00:10:42.070 --> 00:10:44.090
<i>What's the point if you don't enjoy it?</i>

00:10:44.090 --> 00:10:45.330
<i>I guess...</i>

00:10:45.330 --> 00:10:47.010
<i>But what should we do?</i>

00:10:47.750 --> 00:10:50.820
<i>If what you're doing isn't 
fun, then <i>make</i> it fun.</i>

00:10:51.250 --> 00:10:52.440
<i>That's it!</i>

00:10:55.210 --> 00:10:57.510
<b>Ultramarine Alliance</b>

00:11:10.520 --> 00:11:15.270
<b>Ultramarine Alliance</b>

00:11:21.000 --> 00:11:22.500
<i>Yahoo!</i>

00:11:22.500 --> 00:11:24.570
<i>We've finally got a club room!</i>

00:11:24.960 --> 00:11:27.320
<i>Hey, Su-chan! Tone it down a little!</i>

00:11:27.320 --> 00:11:29.730
<i>Jeez, Haru, you're such a handful.</i>

00:11:30.000 --> 00:11:32.930
<i>As of this moment, we of 
the Ultramarine Alliance</i>

00:11:32.930 --> 00:11:35.740
<i>announce the opening of 
the Ultramarine Channel!</i>

00:11:36.170 --> 00:11:39.130
<i>We're gonna let the whole world know that</i>

00:11:39.130 --> 00:11:40.930
<i>we're having more fun than anyone else!</i>

00:11:42.360 --> 00:11:44.680
<i>Yahoo!</i>

00:11:45.800 --> 00:11:47.520
<i>Enjoy your youth!</i>

00:11:46.180 --> 00:11:49.180
<b>Enjoy Your Youth!!</b>

00:11:46.180 --> 00:11:49.180
<b>AquaMine</b>

00:11:47.520 --> 00:11:48.950
<i>AquaMine!</i>

00:11:51.770 --> 00:11:54.470
Maybe they hyped up 
Shirokusa-san too much.

00:11:54.470 --> 00:11:56.220
What, you didn't like it?

00:11:56.220 --> 00:11:58.380
I thought it was fun.

00:11:58.380 --> 00:12:01.500
It was good, especially Sueharu-oniichan.

00:12:01.880 --> 00:12:04.830
I'm glad I didn't end up disappointed.

00:12:04.830 --> 00:12:06.110
Maria...

00:12:06.780 --> 00:12:10.020
I understand their goal of getting the 
Ultramarine Channel's name out there.

00:12:10.020 --> 00:12:10.990
But...

00:12:10.990 --> 00:12:12.070
But?

00:12:12.070 --> 00:12:13.860
That took away its focus.

00:12:13.860 --> 00:12:15.640
It's a commercial for AquaMine,

00:12:15.640 --> 00:12:18.460
but the Ultramarine Channel is what 
makes the biggest impression.

00:12:18.460 --> 00:12:20.360
They got their priorities mixed up.

00:12:20.360 --> 00:12:22.730
I'm pretty sure we're going to win.

00:12:23.120 --> 00:12:25.560
Speaking of making an impression...

00:12:25.560 --> 00:12:28.140
What was that last smile all about?

00:12:35.120 --> 00:12:37.030
<i>Hey, what's up, Momo?</i>

00:12:37.770 --> 00:12:40.610
Sueharu-oniichan, where are you right now?

00:12:41.040 --> 00:12:42.000
<i>Me?</i>

00:12:42.680 --> 00:12:43.670
<i>That's a secret.</i>

00:12:43.670 --> 00:12:44.840
<i>Hey, Sueharu.</i>

00:12:44.840 --> 00:12:48.250
<i>Ma-chan-san says we gotta nail it 
in one or we won't make it in time.</i>

00:12:48.250 --> 00:12:51.440
<i>Oh, sorry, Momo. I'm kinda busy,
 so I gotta go.</i>

00:12:51.440 --> 00:12:52.410
W-Wait—

00:12:52.410 --> 00:12:55.230
<i>Oh, yeah. You've grown into a great actor.</i>

00:12:55.230 --> 00:12:57.250
You watched the commercial?

00:12:57.250 --> 00:13:00.130
<i>After seeing that, I can't let myself lose.</i>

00:13:00.130 --> 00:13:02.520
You still won't admit defeat?

00:13:02.520 --> 00:13:06.030
<i>No way. I'll show you everything 
I've got right now.</i>

00:13:09.060 --> 00:13:10.370
Onii-chan...

00:13:11.720 --> 00:13:13.140
Who was that on the phone?

00:13:13.890 --> 00:13:16.730
The contest isn't over yet.

00:13:16.910 --> 00:13:17.750
Huh?

00:13:21.580 --> 00:13:24.580
Sueharu-oniichan is back.

00:13:30.000 --> 00:13:33.340
Kuro, Shiro... you okay?

00:13:33.340 --> 00:13:34.270
Yeah.

00:13:34.270 --> 00:13:35.880
I'm nervous,

00:13:35.880 --> 00:13:37.970
but more than that, I'm excited.

00:13:38.590 --> 00:13:42.320
I never even dreamed that I'd 
be able to act alongside you.

00:13:42.320 --> 00:13:43.270
Okay.

00:13:45.680 --> 00:13:47.050
We're starting!

00:13:48.950 --> 00:13:50.080
Action!

00:15:08.040 --> 00:15:10.650
This is a continuation of 
the commercial, isn't it?

00:15:10.650 --> 00:15:12.820
They were trying to make the casual,

00:15:12.820 --> 00:15:15.560
everyday theme of the commercial 
feel more precious?

00:15:15.560 --> 00:15:18.580
Sueharu-kun is just too amazing.

00:15:18.580 --> 00:15:20.260
My heart's actually pounding.

00:15:20.700 --> 00:15:23.740
I can't make up a difference like this.

00:15:24.610 --> 00:15:25.800
I...

00:15:27.280 --> 00:15:29.970
can still chase after him.

00:15:29.970 --> 00:15:33.260
I'm not lonely anymore. I'm not alone.

00:15:33.260 --> 00:15:37.750
Because Sueharu-oniichan is 
waiting at the end of my path.

00:15:38.620 --> 00:15:41.120
Maria, I'm happy for you.

00:15:41.640 --> 00:15:42.610
Yeah.

00:15:46.060 --> 00:15:47.880
Cheers!

00:15:49.020 --> 00:15:52.720
Our commercial won easily, 
with more than twice the votes.

00:15:53.070 --> 00:15:55.990
That's so good! Carbs for the win!

00:15:55.990 --> 00:15:59.060
Glad to hear it, Su-chan. 
You haven't eaten for all this time.

00:15:59.540 --> 00:16:01.500
You shouldn't wolf it down, though.

00:16:01.500 --> 00:16:03.690
You're making your big sister worry a bit.

00:16:03.690 --> 00:16:06.380
Hey, he had to lose all that 
weight for the shoot.

00:16:06.380 --> 00:16:07.810
Let him eat all he wants.

00:16:07.820 --> 00:16:15.700
<b>Commercial Contest</b>

00:16:07.820 --> 00:16:15.700
<b>Suggestion from Shirokusa-sama</b>

00:16:07.820 --> 00:16:15.700
<b>\h\h\h\h\hWhile this contest is not intended to obstruct the work of those 
appearing in it, promotion of this commercial at work is prohibited</b>

00:16:08.630 --> 00:16:10.930
You really are a pro, huh?

00:16:10.930 --> 00:16:13.990
The Ultramarine Alliance is 
about having fun, right?

00:16:13.990 --> 00:16:15.700
Giving it your all is what makes it fun.

00:16:15.990 --> 00:16:17.540
How dumb are you, man?

00:16:17.540 --> 00:16:19.320
I don't wanna hear that from you.

00:16:26.670 --> 00:16:30.550
Kai-kun, my dad says he's done 
talking to the principal,

00:16:30.550 --> 00:16:31.830
and he's waiting at the gate.

00:16:35.420 --> 00:16:39.260
This is the course of action I came 
up with for the Ultramarine Alliance.

00:16:39.560 --> 00:16:40.560
Got it.

00:16:42.110 --> 00:16:43.200
Oh, right.

00:16:43.200 --> 00:16:45.690
I took the liberty of looking
 into your background.

00:16:46.590 --> 00:16:48.820
This is why I hate rich people.

00:16:49.040 --> 00:16:52.670
Are you trying to use the Ultramarine 
Alliance as a tool to get revenge

00:16:52.670 --> 00:16:55.790
against Hardy Shun, your father?

00:16:56.550 --> 00:16:58.770
Did you approach Maru-chan because

00:16:58.770 --> 00:17:03.550
he was the top star at the agency your 
despised father is connected to?

00:17:07.100 --> 00:17:10.670
Well, the Ultramarine Alliance 
will be counting on your support.

00:17:10.670 --> 00:17:13.420
I'll take care of all the legal matters.

00:17:13.420 --> 00:17:14.860
See you next time.

00:17:17.260 --> 00:17:19.090
This is why I hate adults.

00:17:19.090 --> 00:17:21.320
I think I hate adults, too.

00:17:22.470 --> 00:17:25.030
I'm sorry. Who are you?

00:17:25.030 --> 00:17:26.600
Strangers are scary.

00:17:26.810 --> 00:17:29.310
I was working on this 
behind the scenes, too,

00:17:29.310 --> 00:17:30.990
so I wanted to know how it ended.

00:17:30.990 --> 00:17:31.940
You were?

00:17:32.210 --> 00:17:34.910
If Hardy Shun were to try anything,

00:17:34.910 --> 00:17:37.520
I was to ask my dad to save you.

00:17:34.950 --> 00:17:39.330
His father is a major player in show business

00:17:34.950 --> 00:17:39.330
<b>Abe Hajime</b>

00:17:37.520 --> 00:17:39.960
What the hell would you 
stand to gain from that?

00:17:39.960 --> 00:17:43.150
Well, I want to see even 
more of Maru-kun in action.

00:17:43.380 --> 00:17:45.930
And? What did you want to know?

00:17:45.930 --> 00:17:48.380
The win and loss records 
of your principal members.

00:17:48.380 --> 00:17:49.890
It can be from your own perspective.

00:17:50.150 --> 00:17:51.970
And what's your judgment?

00:17:51.970 --> 00:17:55.200
Total victory for Maru-kun 
and Shirokusa-chan, I think.

00:17:55.200 --> 00:17:57.520
It boosted both of their 
reputations in the industry.

00:17:57.910 --> 00:18:01.280
It's guaranteed that the scumbag 
president is the only loser here.

00:18:01.280 --> 00:18:04.480
But I think the top winner was Shida-chan,

00:18:04.480 --> 00:18:05.880
with me in second.

00:18:05.880 --> 00:18:08.000
Shida-san was the top winner?

00:18:09.990 --> 00:18:13.560
I don't want Haru to go into show business.

00:18:13.560 --> 00:18:16.300
If you're going to take someone's side,

00:18:16.300 --> 00:18:18.580
it's sure to be the most profitable one.

00:18:19.030 --> 00:18:22.930
And this time, taking my side 
will best serve your purpose.

00:18:22.930 --> 00:18:23.910
Am I wrong?

00:18:23.910 --> 00:18:26.490
You really do have a good eye.

00:18:26.490 --> 00:18:29.820
I want to get Sueharu to 
take part in my plan,

00:18:29.820 --> 00:18:32.510
so I'll be taking your side in this.

00:18:32.970 --> 00:18:35.680
I don't want our goals to end up clashing,

00:18:35.680 --> 00:18:37.360
so let me ask this first.

00:18:37.980 --> 00:18:40.010
What <i>is</i> your goal?

00:18:41.760 --> 00:18:45.750
You're someone who's opposed 
to show business, right?

00:18:46.110 --> 00:18:51.020
I've been thinking that must be 
why you're friends with Haru.

00:18:51.480 --> 00:18:52.870
What makes you think that?

00:18:55.210 --> 00:18:57.910
Just a hunch after seeing 
the way you've acted.

00:18:58.990 --> 00:19:02.060
If you've figured out that much, 
I guess I can tell you a little.

00:19:02.780 --> 00:19:05.350
The president of Sueharu's 
agency is a scumbag.

00:19:05.730 --> 00:19:07.850
I kinda have a connection to him.

00:19:08.290 --> 00:19:09.130
That's it.

00:19:11.220 --> 00:19:14.030
I'm going to pretend I have amnesia.

00:19:14.250 --> 00:19:15.200
Huh?

00:19:15.460 --> 00:19:18.550
It's cowardly, but I think 
it's the best option.

00:19:19.130 --> 00:19:23.300
If I have amnesia, Haru will try to help me.

00:19:23.300 --> 00:19:25.770
Then, if I take my time 
getting closer to him,

00:19:25.770 --> 00:19:26.920
I can erase his trauma.

00:19:27.620 --> 00:19:29.260
You think you can do that?

00:19:29.550 --> 00:19:31.510
It's not about whether I can or can't.

00:19:31.510 --> 00:19:32.350
I'm going to.

00:19:32.790 --> 00:19:35.670
If Haru goes to meet with 
that agency president,

00:19:35.670 --> 00:19:37.460
I plan to go with him.

00:19:37.780 --> 00:19:39.600
Haru hates it when people are 
mean to those close to him

00:19:39.600 --> 00:19:41.880
even more than when they're mean to him,

00:19:41.880 --> 00:19:45.290
so if the president is a 
scumbag like you say,

00:19:45.290 --> 00:19:47.230
he's bound to say some nasty things.

00:19:47.230 --> 00:19:49.440
If that happens, his return to 
acting is dead in the water.

00:19:50.010 --> 00:19:55.460
Sueharu was so scared of Shida-chan, 
but suddenly he's back to normal.

00:19:55.460 --> 00:19:58.880
Kachi had a huge advantage, 
but now they're both even.

00:19:59.260 --> 00:20:02.520
No matter how you look at it, 
Shida-chan's the winner.

00:20:02.520 --> 00:20:03.720
True.

00:20:03.720 --> 00:20:07.530
And I don't need to explain 
why I'm second, right?

00:20:07.530 --> 00:20:10.250
Just look at how the Ultramarine 
Alliance came together.

00:20:10.250 --> 00:20:12.660
I will say that you did a great job there.

00:20:13.090 --> 00:20:15.920
And there's one more who 
won big in all this.

00:20:17.250 --> 00:20:18.610
So anyway,

00:20:18.610 --> 00:20:22.080
I'm Momosaka Maria, and I've just 
transferred to this school.

00:20:22.080 --> 00:20:23.700
I'm glad to meet you!

00:20:23.700 --> 00:20:25.150
What?!

00:20:25.360 --> 00:20:27.190
What's the meaning of this, Su-chan?!

00:20:27.190 --> 00:20:28.860
Haru, explain!

00:20:28.860 --> 00:20:32.640
Sueharu-oniichan said he wanted me here.

00:20:32.640 --> 00:20:35.170
No, no! Momo asked me to save her!

00:20:35.170 --> 00:20:37.440
She wanted to be rescued 
from that president!

00:20:37.440 --> 00:20:38.720
No, I didn't.

00:20:39.600 --> 00:20:42.600
Although I did get along 
poorly with Shun-san,

00:20:42.600 --> 00:20:45.270
so it's true that the timing was perfect.

00:20:45.270 --> 00:20:47.120
Huh? Wait, what are you saying?

00:20:48.500 --> 00:20:51.060
I was just starved for love!

00:20:51.670 --> 00:20:54.090
So I used quitting the 
agency as an opportunity

00:20:54.090 --> 00:20:57.310
to rely on you to get me 
transferred into this school!

00:20:57.830 --> 00:21:02.630
I hardly got to attend school at all while 
I was acting, so I'm really excited!

00:21:03.380 --> 00:21:06.060
Let's continue to be good friends, okay,

00:21:06.280 --> 00:21:07.620
Senpai?

00:21:09.090 --> 00:21:10.430
Huh?!

00:21:11.330 --> 00:21:13.670
Oops! Forgot I had something to do...

00:21:14.030 --> 00:21:15.180
Su-chan!

00:21:15.180 --> 00:21:16.580
Stop right there!

00:21:18.970 --> 00:21:20.660
If you want Paisen, he's over there.

00:21:20.660 --> 00:21:21.580
Thanks!

00:21:21.800 --> 00:21:23.160
All good, Paisen.

00:21:24.690 --> 00:21:26.290
You saved my skin, Rena.

00:21:26.290 --> 00:21:28.820
For an older kid, you're a 
real handful, you know that?

00:21:32.640 --> 00:21:36.320
By the way, Paisen, why are you 
friends with Tetsu-senpai?

00:21:36.320 --> 00:21:37.640
All you guys do is fight.

00:21:37.640 --> 00:21:39.500
Huh? Oh...

00:21:39.500 --> 00:21:42.950
Well, when most people find 
out I was a child actor,

00:21:42.950 --> 00:21:45.030
they expect me to do something for them.

00:21:45.300 --> 00:21:46.690
But Tetsuhiko...

00:21:47.350 --> 00:21:49.990
He's the only one who tries 
to do stuff <i>with</i> me.

00:21:49.990 --> 00:21:53.090
Basically, he stands beside me.

00:21:53.520 --> 00:21:55.780
That's why we're friends.

00:21:56.700 --> 00:22:00.300
You and Tetsu-senpai are kind of alike, huh?

00:22:00.300 --> 00:22:03.550
Don't say he and I are alike,
 even as a joke!

00:22:03.550 --> 00:22:05.030
That actually hurts!

00:22:05.030 --> 00:22:06.840
Wow, you're a pain.

00:22:06.840 --> 00:22:08.140
Found you, Haru!

00:22:08.140 --> 00:22:08.920
Kuro!

00:22:21.890 --> 00:22:25.010
Haru, dinner tonight is 
Hamburg steaks, apparently.

00:22:25.220 --> 00:22:27.390
That's your favorite, right? Aren't you lucky?

00:22:27.390 --> 00:22:29.380
Seriously? I want some!

00:22:33.760 --> 00:22:36.990
Oh, and she says I'm getting 
corn soup with watermelon!

00:22:36.990 --> 00:22:38.430
Yay! My favorite!

00:22:38.430 --> 00:22:39.160
Huh?

00:22:39.730 --> 00:22:41.790
Kuro, your sense of taste is back?

00:22:41.790 --> 00:22:44.140
Huh? Oh... Oh, yeah!

00:22:44.140 --> 00:22:46.120
My sense of taste changed, didn't it?

00:22:46.120 --> 00:22:48.910
That's been my favorite for a long time,
 so I was involuntarily happy.

00:22:48.910 --> 00:22:50.800
Whoopsie.

00:22:50.800 --> 00:22:52.980
What the heck, Kuro? You're such a klutz.

00:22:53.510 --> 00:22:57.250
I'm still a whole lot less 
klutzy than you are.

00:22:57.750 --> 00:23:00.190
Yes, yes, you're right.

00:23:00.420 --> 00:23:04.680
You made a ton of careless 
mistakes on the last quiz.

00:23:04.680 --> 00:23:06.790
Aren't your grades kind of in danger?

00:23:08.350 --> 00:23:11.110
And yours have stayed near 
the top this whole time.

00:23:11.110 --> 00:23:12.390
It's amazing.

00:23:12.390 --> 00:23:14.190
It's a difference in effort.

00:23:14.190 --> 00:23:17.090
You were always sleeping 
through our summer classes.

00:23:17.090 --> 00:23:18.350
I saw you.

00:23:18.890 --> 00:23:20.350
Huh? Kuro...

00:23:20.760 --> 00:23:24.870
How can you remember our summer 
classes if you have amnesia?

00:23:36.050 --> 00:23:37.690
Kuro!
